  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CDT Wed Jul 1 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will begin to weaken and drift eastward on \nIndependence Day. Temperatures will be a couple degrees cooler, but \nthe heat will still be dangerous with heat indices in the 100-110\nrange. Scattered storms will develop during the afternoon with \ncoverage decreasing after dark. The ridge will move further east \non Sunday with highs in the low to mid 90s. PoPs will increase as \nwell. The trend will carry into next week as a trough sets up in \nthe plains and Mississippi River valley. We'll see daily medium \nstorm chances with highs back to normal in the mid 80s to low 90s \nby midweek.",
